# Redshirt Sports: core rules

This repo is the live Redshirt Sports site. `docs/blueprint/` (v1.7, handoff edition) is the **target architecture**. We **evolve this repo incrementally**: the site stays live, nothing gets rebuilt from scratch, and any URL that moves gets a one-time legacy 301. Work milestone by milestone from `docs/blueprint/BUILD_ORDER.md`, starting with Milestone 0 (the audit). Local development only: see `01-local-only.mdc`.

## Before writing code
- Read the relevant `docs/blueprint/NN-*.md` section and `CONTEXT.md`, the domain glossary (School, Browse Scope, Poll, Ballot, Rankings, Week…). Use its terms in code and copy.
- Next.js, Turborepo, Sanity and Clerk move fast. Check the installed versions' docs (`node_modules/next/dist/docs/`, the turbo package's `docs/`) and the skills in `.agents/skills/` before using an API. Leave the tool-managed blocks in `AGENTS.md` and `apps/web/AGENTS.md` alone.
- The repo's names win over the blueprint's: `@rs/*` in the docs means the existing `@redshirt-sports/*` package; `supabase/migrations` means `apps/web/supabase/migrations`; `pnpm typecheck` means `pnpm check:types`.
- One milestone = one PR on a feature branch. Never push to `main`.

## Stack (do not swap any of these)
- **Next.js App Router** (Cache Components: `"use cache"`, `cacheTag`, `cacheLife`; Server Components by default), React 19, TypeScript.
- **Turborepo + pnpm** workspaces, with the version catalog in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. Biome for lint/format, Vitest for tests.
- **Tailwind CSS v4, CSS-first**: tokens live in `packages/ui/src/styles/globals.css` (`@theme inline`, oklch). **No `tailwind.config.*`** and no hard-coded hex colors in components.
- **shadcn/ui** components in `packages/ui`, via `components.json`.
- **Drizzle ORM** for all Postgres access (schema in `packages/db`, migrations from drizzle-kit). **Supabase Postgres with RLS** on every table (deny by default).
- **Clerk** for auth (roles in metadata, webhooks via svix).
- **Sanity** for content (schemas in `apps/studio/schemaTypes`, GROQ in `packages/sanity`, typegen). **`sanity-image`** for images: no custom `next/image` Sanity loader.

## URL and routing rules (non-negotiable)
- **Zero rewrites.** No `rewrites()` in any `next.config`, no `NextResponse.rewrite`, no proxy routes. App Router folders map 1:1 to public URLs.
- **The only redirects allowed are one-time permanent (301/308) legacy redirects** from old Redshirt URLs (blueprint §27). No slug-change, "latest", `?page=1`, case-normalization or role-based redirects: render in place, set a canonical, or 404. Sign-in protection by Clerk is the one auth exception.
- Pagination is **`?page=n`** only: page 1 has no param, every page self-canonicalizes, there is no rel prev/next, and an invalid page returns 404. Never `/page/n`.
- **Level → sport URLs (v1.6):** `/college` is a real level hub page, with `/college/news`, `/college/football/…`, `/college/mens-basketball/…` and `/college/womens-basketball/…`. `/high-school/…` is a reserved future level: don't build it. Never create the pre-1.6 single-segment sport roots (see the Changes in 1.6 note). Build every path with the `urls` helper and `sportBase()`.
- Team hubs: `/teams/{school-nickname}`. A school with no nickname (Hollins, slug `hollins`) keeps a single-token slug. Voting target: **`apps/vote` at `vote.redshirtsports.com`** (today it lives at `/vote` in `apps/web`; don't add new voting surfaces to www).

## Product scope: refuse to build
- No game, score, standings or schedule data products. No live blogs (`*/live/*`), rosters, player pages or player DBs. Outbound link cards instead (§15). The ESPN client is for the poll week calendar only.
- **No fan vote** and no fan-built Top 25 (removed in v1.5). The only Top 25 is the credentialed voters' poll.
- **No comments or forums.** No sign-in modals on page load or first article view.
- No portal or recruiting databases, feeds or scrapers. The Transfer Portal Tracker is editor-maintained Sanity `portalEntry` docs.

## Transfer Portal Tracker (flags)
- **In scope. Build the UI from `docs/mockups/portal-tracker.html` and `portal-tracker-*.png`.** Decision #17 is closed: that uploaded mockup is the design.
- **The story link is optional (Decision #16).** Studio warns, it does not block publish. The row shows "No story yet" when `story` is empty. Never hide or reject an entry for a missing story.

## Images
- Serve **AVIF/WebP** (`auto=format`, the `sanity-image` default). Keep the largest rendered image **under 200 KB** (quality around 75), set width/height, keep hotspot/crop, add LQIP to heroes, and never upscale. Static assets are committed as WebP/AVIF under 200 KB.

## Done means
- `pnpm lint`, `pnpm check:types` and the relevant `pnpm test` pass. DB changes come with a generated migration and RLS tests.
- `rg -n "rewrites|NextResponse.rewrite" apps packages` returns nothing.
- The PR description lists which blueprint section and acceptance boxes it satisfies.
